Menu confirm: accept the power key (SCAN_SUSPEND) as confirm

Upstream inconsistency: UniXNUMenuConfirm draws the footer "Power key =
confirm" (or "Power key: confirm" when choices are shown), but its accept
set only contains CR/LF. The power key reaches the menu as SCAN_SUSPEND
(ButtonsDxe, stock flashlmdd key translation) and therefore fell through
to the catch-all cancel at the bottom of the loop -- the exact opposite of
what the footer promises, and user-visible as soon as physical keys work
(menu-physical-keys.patch).

Fix: one condition -- add (Key.ScanCode == SCAN_SUSPEND) to the confirm
accept set in UniXNUMenuConfirm. Nothing else changes; with choices shown,
SCAN_SUSPEND confirms the highlighted choice exactly like Enter, including
the highlighted-Cancel case.

Applies on top of menu-physical-keys.patch (build-tree Menu.c blob
d3e1e20). Archived for flashlm as UniXNU-flashlm
patches/menu-confirm-suspend.patch.

diff --git a/package/UniXNUPkg/Library/UniXNULib/Menu.c b/package/UniXNUPkg/Library/UniXNULib/Menu.c
index d3e1e20..c90536d 100644
--- a/package/UniXNUPkg/Library/UniXNULib/Menu.c
+++ b/package/UniXNUPkg/Library/UniXNULib/Menu.c
@@ -560,7 +560,13 @@ UniXNUMenuConfirm (
       }
     }
 
-    if ((Key.UnicodeChar == CHAR_CARRIAGE_RETURN) || (Key.UnicodeChar == CHAR_LINEFEED)) {
+    //
+    // flashlm: the prompt's footer promises "Power key = confirm", but upstream's
+    // accept set only had CR/LF, so the power key (SCAN_SUSPEND from
+    // ButtonsDxe) fell through to cancel. Accept it here to match the footer.
+    //
+    if ((Key.UnicodeChar == CHAR_CARRIAGE_RETURN) || (Key.UnicodeChar == CHAR_LINEFEED) ||
+        (Key.ScanCode == SCAN_SUSPEND)) {
       if (Items > 0) {
         if (Shown + 1 == Items) {
           return FALSE;
